{
  "description": "Shared webhook signature vectors. The API signer and every SDK verify-and-parse helper must pass all of them. Scheme: Standard Webhooks v1, signature = 'v1,' + base64(HMAC-SHA256(base64decode(secret without 'whsec_'), id + '.' + timestamp + '.' + body)). 'now' is the clock value the verifier must use; default tolerance is 300 seconds. Rules the vectors pin down: header names are matched case-insensitively; the same header given twice with different values is rejected (ambiguous_header); the timestamp is 1 to 12 ASCII digits and nothing else; the clock is truncated to whole seconds before comparing; base64 (secret and signatures) is the standard alphabet, padded, with no whitespace; the decoded key must not be empty; the body must be exactly one JSON object; a known event type must carry an object in `data` with its required fields; an unknown type is returned as-is.",
